<!--
  What has to be in ios/Runner/Info.plist for NOKTA.

  It is a short list on purpose. The guest app has no local-network discovery,
  no Bonjour service and no camera, so none of the keys the waiter app needs
  apply here - and every one of them omitted is one fewer permission prompt and
  one fewer question at review.

  `bash tools/ios-izinler.sh` writes all of this with PlistBuddy after
  `flutter create --platforms=ios .` on the Mac. This file is the record of
  what that script writes.
-->

<key>CFBundleDisplayName</key>
<string>NOKTA</string>

<key>UIUserInterfaceStyle</key>
<string>Dark</string>

<!-- Portrait only. This is a card held up at a counter; there is nothing on
     any screen that a landscape phone shows better. -->
<key>UISupportedInterfaceOrientations</key>
<array>
  <string>UIInterfaceOrientationPortrait</string>
</array>
